# v4 (RF-DETR) checkpoint -- 352MB, exceeds GitHub's 100MB per-file limit. v3 (pose-based) is the
# active fall-detection pipeline and doesn't need this file. v4's code is kept for anyone with GPU
# access who wants to use it, but they'll need to source this checkpoint separately.
models/rfdetr_fall_detector.pth

# YOLO checkpoints downloaded ad hoc while benchmarking pose-extractor/detector candidates
# (SS34/35) -- not used by the app, and yolo26x.pt alone is 113MB, over GitHub's non-LFS limit.
# The one YOLO-pose checkpoint the app actually loads lives at models/yolo26s-pose.pt instead.
training/*.pt
/yolov10x.pt

# Raw/intermediate training data (downloaded datasets, extracted pose features, model download
# caches) -- 2.4GB+, none of it needed to just run the app. The trained model files under models/
# already have the learned weights baked in; this is only needed if someone wants to retrain from
# scratch, which is out of scope for "clone and run."
training/data/
training/models_cache/

# Runtime-generated alert snapshot images (app/services/alert_service.py saves a
# frame here on every fall_red/alone_yellow alert) -- not source, regenerated on use.
/tmp/